  "confidence": "high",
  "notes": "Page 5-1 of the M5200A manual. Note on the page: connectors J1 to J6 wired identical. Pin order read from the lead lines: left labels go to 1-19, right labels to 20-37. The SELECT bracket on the left covers STROBE 3, STROBE 1, NALE5 and NRD; on the right STROBE 4, 2, 0 and NWR. DATA A / DATA B are 8-bit buses (even bits on 10-13/15-18, odd bits on 28-31/33-36); ports keyed D0-D7. Directions (select/strobe/NRD/NWR as control_out, data as bus) are inferred from the signal names, not stated. Typical mating connector P1: T&B/Ansley 609-37P (male 37 pin 'D'), 609-037 backshell, 609-004A jackscrew set. Legend: NC not connected, IC internally connected."
}
